```
  Detection : Microsoft Office application spawning a shell / script host
  MITRE     : T1566.001 Phishing: Spearphishing Attachment
              T1204.002 User Execution: Malicious File
  Data      : Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Create)
  Why       : Word or Excel should almost never launch cmd, PowerShell or mshta.
              When they do, a malicious macro is the most likely cause.
  Severity  : High
  Author    : Ifeanyi Solomon Uneze
```
index=sysmon EventCode=1
    ParentImage IN ("*\\winword.exe", "*\\excel.exe", "*\\powerpnt.exe", "*\\outlook.exe", "*\\onenote.exe")
    Image IN ("*\\cmd.exe", "*\\powershell.exe", "*\\pwsh.exe", "*\\wscript.exe", "*\\cscript.exe",
              "*\\mshta.exe", "*\\rundll32.exe", "*\\regsvr32.exe", "*\\certutil.exe")
| stats count min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        values(CommandLine) AS command_lines
        BY host User ParentImage Image
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - count

```
  TRIAGE
  1. Which document was open? Check ParentCommandLine for the file path.
  2. Find the email that delivered it (message trace by recipient + time).
  3. Did the child process download anything? (Sysmon EID 3 / EID 11)
  4. Search all hosts for the same document name or hash: was it sent to others?

  TUNING
  - Some add-ins legitimately call cmd.exe. Allow-list by exact CommandLine.
```
